    "lines": [
      {
        "y": 11.4,
        "x0": 33.2,
        "x1": 72.2,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "66"
      },
      {
        "y": 23.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 308,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "Speed: fast and slow"
      },
      {
        "y": 70.5,
        "x0": 75.1,
        "x1": 154.8,
        "tag": "title",
        "text": "A Going fast"
      },
      {
        "y": 88,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 495.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "These verbs suggest going somewhere very quickly on foot or in a vehicle: dash, fly, race, tear."
      },
      {
        "y": 100,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I dashed into the classroom to pick up my books. She came flying out of her house. I raced/tore to"
      },
      {
        "y": 112.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 316.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "the station and just made it in time for the last train."
      },
      {
        "y": 128.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 492.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The verbs nip and pop suggest going a short distance quickly, on foot or in a vehicle: I nipped/"
      },
      {
        "y": 140.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 316.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "popped into a near by shop to buy a bottle of water."
      },
      {
        "y": 156.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 499.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The verb dart suggests a quick, sudden movement, often by an animal: A dragonfly darted past."
      },
      {
        "y": 168.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 237.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "I darted behind the door to hide."
      },
      {
        "y": 184.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The verbs zip and whizz are often used about vehicles going quickly: The bus whizzed/zipped past"
      },
      {
        "y": 197.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 228.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "me just as I got to the bus stop."
      },
      {
        "y": 213,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 473.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The verb bolt also suggests fast movement over a short distance but it also has the added"
      },
      {
        "y": 225,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 475.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "association of running away from something: The thieves bolted when the alarm went off."
      },
      {
        "y": 241.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 519.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The verb career suggests that something is moving rapidly and is out of control: The car skidded and"
      },
      {
        "y": 253.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 430.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "careered down a bank. The company seems to be careering into financial ruin."
      },
      {
        "y": 269.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 519.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The verbs scamper, scurry, scuttle suggest small rapid steps, often used to describe the way a small"
      },
      {
        "y": 281.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 509.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "animal runs: As we went into the dark shed, we saw mice scampering away and spiders scurrying"
      },
      {
        "y": 293.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 346.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "into corners. Cockroaches scuttled into a crack in the floor."
      },
      {
        "y": 309.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 506.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "These verbs emphasise the fact that speed is increasing: speed up, accelerate. Accelerate is used"
      },
      {
        "y": 321.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 518.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "only about transport, whereas speed up can also refer to movement on foot. Both verbs can be used"
      },
      {
        "y": 333.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 519.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "figuratively: We’d better speed up if we’re going to get there on time. The growth of the company has"
      },
      {
        "y": 345.8,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 258,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "accelerated since it started exporting."
      },
      {
        "y": 367.1,
        "x0": 74.7,
        "x1": 220.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "B Going up or down fast"
      },
      {
        "y": 384.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 490.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "These verbs suggest a downward movement, as well as speed: plunge, plummet: He put on a"
      },
      {
        "y": 396.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 501.3,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "lifejacket and plunged into the icy water. Notice that they are mainly used metaphorically: When"
      },
      {
        "y": 408.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 495.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "export sales began to decline, our hopes of business success plummeted. After the death of his"
      },
      {
        "y": 420.6,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 249.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "father, he was plunged into despair."
      },
      {
        "y": 436.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 486.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "These verbs suggest a fast upward movement: rocket, soar. Notice that they are mainly used"
      },
      {
        "y": 449.3,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 513.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "metaphorically and have strong associations with financial matters such as prices and share values:"
      },
      {
        "y": 460.9,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 314.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "When our export sales rocketed, our hopes soared."
      },
      {
        "y": 477.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 476.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The primary association of soar is with birds, and when it is used about people’s feelings it"
      },
      {
        "y": 489.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 486.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "provides associations of happiness and being carefree: My heart soared when I heard that he"
      },
      {
        "y": 501.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 177.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "was coming home."
      },
      {
        "y": 517.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "The opposite of soar and rocket in a financial context would be slump or tumble. Both suggest a"
      },
      {
        "y": 529.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 512.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "rapid downward movement: Share prices slumped (or plummeted) on the stock market yesterday,"
      },
      {
        "y": 541.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 399,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "with telecommunications companies tumbling most dramatically of all."
      },
      {
        "y": 562.7,
        "x0": 75,
        "x1": 169.9,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "C Going slowly"
      },
      {
        "y": 580.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 504.6,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "These intransitive verbs emphasise that the movement is slow: crawl, creep. They are often used"
      },
      {
        "y": 592.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 485,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "metaphorically: Prices have been creeping up since May. It was rush hour and the traffic was"
      },
      {
        "y": 604.2,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 165.5,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "crawling along."
      },
      {
        "y": 620.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 511.4,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Totter also suggests a fairly slow movement, but it is one that is particularly unsteady as well: Mina"
      },
      {
        "y": 632.5,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 322.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "tottered down the road, laden with parcels and bags."
      },
      {
        "y": 648.7,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 497.1,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Sidle means to walk anxiously and nervously: Sam sidled up to the boss’s desk and coughed to"
      },
      {
        "y": 661.1,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 184.2,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "attract his attention."
      },
      {
        "y": 677,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 488.7,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "Dawdle means to move more slowly than is necessary, or to waste time: Don’t dawdle on the"
      },
      {
        "y": 689.4,
        "x0": 99.2,
        "x1": 144.8,
        "tag": "main",
        "text": "way home."
      }
    ],
